<![CDATA[&Bpara_group&C&Bp&C&G&Bpara_align&C3&B/para_align&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type=&Etitle_region&E&C&Bmain_tag&C&B![CDATA[page_title]]&C&B/main_tag&C&F&G&Bpara_group&C&Bp&C&G&Bpara_align&C3&B/para_align&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E13&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Ehaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E11558199&E si=&E1&E sm=&E4506&E ss=&Eh1&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E13&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Ehaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E11558199&E si=&E1&E sm=&E4506&E ss=&Eh1&E&C&Bitem type = &Enormal&E&C&B![CDATA[Reading vapour fraction]]&C&B/item&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&B/p&C&G&B/para_group&C&B/item&C&B/p&C&G&Bp&C&G&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&Bitem type = &Enormal&E&C&B![CDATA[When a compound is in the liquid-vapor dome, it is often useful to know what fraction of the compound is in a saturated liquid state and what fraction is in a saturated vapor state. The term, vapor fraction, gives the fraction that is in a gaseous state. Vapor fraction is represented by the variable, x.]]&C&B/item&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&B/p&C&G&Bp&C&G&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&B/p&C&G&Bp&C&G&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&Bitem type = &Enormal&E&C&B![CDATA[The line left of the critical point on the dome is the saturated liquid line. That means the vapor fraction anywhere on that line is 0. However, the line to the right on the dome is the saturated vapor line. That means the vapor fraction on that line is 1. Any point between those too lines then has a vapor fraction value between 0 and 1.]]&C&B/item&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&B/p&C&G&Bp&C&G&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&B/p&C&G&Bp&C&G&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epara_start&E/&C&Bfield id = &E0&E data = &ENO_DATA&E&C&Bfont v=&E2&E h=&E11&E w=&E0&E chs=&E1&E d=&Eeaaaaa&E fc=&EArial&E cl=&E0&E si=&E0&E sm=&E4490&E ss=&Enormal&E&C&B/font&C&B/field&C&Bitem type = &Epicture&E&C&Bsealed&C1&B/sealed&C&Bnormal&C1&B/normal&C&Badd&C1&B/add&C&Buseprop&C0&B/useprop&C&Bborderwidth&C0&B/borderwidth&C&Bmargin_left&C0&B/margin_left&C&Bmargin_right&C0&B/margin_right&C&Bmargin_top&C0&B/margin_top&C&Bmargin_bottom&C0&B/margin_bottom&C&Bscalex&C1.0000000000&B/scalex&C&Bscaley&C1.0000000000&B/scaley&C&Bwidth&C360&B/width&C&Bheight&C320&B/height&C&Bscreen_bits&C&B![CDATA[iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAWgAAAFACAYAAACRGuaOAAAABmJLR0QA/wD/AP+gvaeTAAAACXBI&GWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAe+0lEQVR4nO3dL1giffv+8dPf8Q3YsGmcbWyDpnFsbsMmEZrbsGlk&Gmza3SXSbtLVJlAZN2hK1QYM2v+DD3AMO/2fgGni/jmO